{"name":"Cream Puff","hex":"#ffbb99","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cream puff","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light, hollow pastry typically filled with cream or custard.","A weak or ineffectual person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream_puff"}],"entries":[{"title":"Profiterole","blocks":[{"text":"A profiterole, or chou à la crème, known as a cream puff in the US and Canada, is a filled French choux pastry ball with a typically sweet and moist filling of whipped cream, custard, pastry cream, or ice cream. They may be garnished with chocolate sauce, caramel, or a dusting of powdered sugar."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Paris_2e_-_Rue_Vivienne_-_Restaurant_Le_Vaudeville_-_Profiteroles_au_chocolat.jpg/330px-Paris_2e_-_Rue_Vivienne_-_Restaurant_Le_Vaudeville_-_Profiteroles_au_chocolat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Profiterole","wikidata":"Q1152821"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream","wikidata":"Q13228"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2730433"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Profiteroles_by_Star5112.jpg/120px-Profiteroles_by_Star5112.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Profiteroles_by_Star5112.jpg/250px-Profiteroles_by_Star5112.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Profiteroles_by_Star5112.jpg/120px-Profiteroles_by_Star5112.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AProfiteroles_by_Star5112.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Windbeutel.jpg/120px-Windbeutel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Windbeutel.jpg/250px-Windbeutel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Windbeutel.jpg/120px-Windbeutel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWindbeutel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/V%C4%9ATRN%C3%8DK_%2B%C5%A1X%C3%A9%C5%99X%C4%9B%C3%A9%C4%9B%C3%A9.jpg/120px-V%C4%9ATRN%C3%8DK_%2B%C5%A1X%C3%A9%C5%99X%C